From: Basem Barakat <basem.barakay@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:53:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [ROCm][Perf][MoE] Trim MoRI dispatch output to rows that
 can hold a token

MoRI's dispatch() returns its whole preallocated receive buffer,
num_dispatchers * max_num_tokens rows, regardless of how many tokens
arrived. The modular kernel sizes the expert GEMMs from that row count,
so a decode step with one token per rank runs the experts over the full
prefill-sized buffer (8192 rows at EP8 with max_num_batched_tokens=1024).

Each source rank sends a destination at most one copy of each of its
tokens, and received tokens are packed from row 0, so no more than
num_dispatchers * max(tokens on any DP rank) rows can be live. Slice the
dispatched activations, ids, weights and scales to that bound. The bound
comes from DPMetadata.num_tokens_across_dp_cpu, so it is host-side and
cudagraph-safe; when it covers the whole buffer (prefill, profile_run)
nothing is sliced, and without DP metadata the buffer is left as is.

DeepSeek-V4-Flash, 2P/2D EP16 PD disaggregation, MI300X, 1024/1024:
TPOT 855 ms -> 30 ms at concurrency 1, 863 -> 35 ms at 16.

Signed-off-by: Basem Barakat <basem.barakay@amd.com>
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
---
 .../layers/fused_moe/prepare_finalize/mori.py | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/prepare_finalize/mori.py b/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/prepare_finalize/mori.py
index 53427f2de..375b64bc5 100644
--- a/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/prepare_finalize/mori.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/prepare_finalize/mori.py
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@ import mori
 import torch
 
 import vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.modular_kernel as mk
+from vllm.forward_context import get_forward_context, is_forward_context_available
 from vllm.logger import init_logger
 from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.config import FusedMoEQuantConfig
 from vllm.platforms import current_platform
@@ -51,6 +52,27 @@ class MoriPrepareAndFinalize(mk.FusedMoEPrepareAndFinalizeModular):
     def supports_async(self) -> bool:
         return False
 
+    def _num_live_dispatch_rows(self, num_local_tokens: int, num_rows: int) -> int:
+        """Rows of the dispatch output that can hold a received token.
+
+        dispatch() returns MoRI's whole receive buffer, sized
+        num_dispatchers * max_tokens_per_rank, and the modular kernel sizes
+        the expert GEMMs from its row count. Each source rank sends this rank
+        at most one copy of each of its tokens, and received tokens are packed
+        from row 0, so only num_dispatchers * (max tokens on any rank) rows
+        can be live. The bound has to cover every source rank, so it comes
+        from the DP token counts rather than this rank's batch alone.
+        """
+        if not is_forward_context_available():
+            return num_rows
+        dp_metadata = get_forward_context().dp_metadata
+        if dp_metadata is None:
+            return num_rows
+        max_tokens = max(
+            int(dp_metadata.num_tokens_across_dp_cpu.max()), num_local_tokens
+        )
+        return min(self.num_dispatchers_ * max_tokens, num_rows)
+
     def prepare(
         self,
         a1: torch.Tensor,
@@ -118,6 +140,15 @@ class MoriPrepareAndFinalize(mk.FusedMoEPrepareAndFinalizeModular):
             dispatch_recv_token_num,
         ) = self.mori_op.dispatch(a1, topk_weights, scale, topk_ids)
 
+        num_rows = self._num_live_dispatch_rows(a1.shape[0], dispatch_a1.shape[0])
+        if num_rows < dispatch_a1.shape[0]:
+            dispatch_a1 = dispatch_a1[:num_rows]
+            dispatch_ids = dispatch_ids[:num_rows]
+            if dispatch_weights is not None:
+                dispatch_weights = dispatch_weights[:num_rows]
+            if dispatch_scale is not None:
+                dispatch_scale = dispatch_scale[:num_rows]
+
         expert_tokens_meta = mk.ExpertTokensMetadata(
             expert_num_tokens=dispatch_recv_token_num, expert_num_tokens_cpu=None
         )
